# === SECRETS — never bake these into an image (esp. a public one) ===
# Root cause of the recurring GCP key compromise: `COPY . .` with no
# .dockerignore published .env (and a GCP SA key) into public Docker Hub layers.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
service_account_key.json
*_key.json
*-key.json
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Kubernetes overlays that hold real secrets (deployed overlay is gitignored)
k8s/overlays/deployed/

# Local tooling / agent settings that may contain tokens
.claude/settings.local.json

# === Other services' build contexts — NOT part of the bot image ===
# The bot image is built from the repo root, so `COPY . .` swallows both Python
# sidecars, including their local virtualenvs (~1.4GB of agent-sidecar/ +
# voice-sidecar/). They are separate images with their own Dockerfiles and are
# never executed from the bot container. Excluding them is the same COPY-everything
# hygiene that the secrets block above exists for -- that one leaked credentials,
# this one leaks build weight into a PUBLIC image.
agent-sidecar/
voice-sidecar/
**/venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The SDD/audit scratch workspace (git-ignored, but the build context sees it).
.superpowers/

# === Build hygiene (not secrets, just don't belong in the image) ===
.git
.gitignore
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
__tests__
coverage
*.md
docs/
scratchpad/
.DS_Store
